[{:db/id "q-74348/selection/35a9c70cb56f504b5cc7db1b0bed29aa1b57f457981fc5a5955537178f4eea4a" :answer/id #uuid "bc1cfce2-6c67-5656-87bc-be24f48eda93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74348/selection/5a03cb687b07e0d02c33a49ba5fce913f192f07a178da933b5403fee82e9240a" :answer/id #uuid "ddbba9c1-d208-5e0d-9a78-34e013b77432" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "29.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74348/selection/d3f73c8b9a627fc347c07c88f346634bb3a6e77c4d4845938f6892904568ded2" :answer/id #uuid "650f6364-88bd-507c-acb9-321b25deaf37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74348/selection/5e30bd0dd4c2c1ef7ccd8cd95de176527399713c97b88bb0b2643355798e6f6b" :answer/id #uuid "dc228cb9-000b-5a1b-be3b-3059a46fc7c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32.55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74348/selection/af47ee73c59bbde931006c9a1a7a49a1285419a4462334bf71c227dffcaad797" :answer/id #uuid "a9f63acf-8db0-5178-8632-91127264c441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74348/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a99f58-21b0-5f70-be82-6f1b49360c42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74348/selection/35a9c70cb56f504b5cc7db1b0bed29aa1b57f457981fc5a5955537178f4eea4a" :answer-field/choices ["q-74348/selection/35a9c70cb56f504b5cc7db1b0bed29aa1b57f457981fc5a5955537178f4eea4a" "q-74348/selection/5a03cb687b07e0d02c33a49ba5fce913f192f07a178da933b5403fee82e9240a" "q-74348/selection/d3f73c8b9a627fc347c07c88f346634bb3a6e77c4d4845938f6892904568ded2" "q-74348/selection/5e30bd0dd4c2c1ef7ccd8cd95de176527399713c97b88bb0b2643355798e6f6b" "q-74348/selection/af47ee73c59bbde931006c9a1a7a49a1285419a4462334bf71c227dffcaad797"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74348" :question/id #uuid "db39980f-8283-5ef8-83b5-f354ae931bda" :question/math-academy-id "q-74348" :question/problem "The following table shows the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the interval $[4,9].$\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $5.5$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $4$ | $6$ | $9.5$ |\n\nUse the right Riemann sum, with the three subintervals indicated by the data, to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ over the interval $[4,9].$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈f(5.5)Δ{x}_{1}+f(8)Δ{x}_{2}+f(9)Δ{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $5.5$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $-$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ | $1$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $4$ | $6$ | $9.5$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈4\\cdot 1.5+6\\cdot 2.5+9.5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6+15+9.5 \\\\  & =30.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74348/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecb9df79-5227-5fc6-9a20-818fee34e971"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74348"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "adc3ca3f-6f32-5621-aeca-a53b4820ba3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "4b11eb67-5db6-584c-bae9-3d6d0d845c49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "94e554a5-29ef-5d6a-9778-0f1c7aaa6c9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "da45de20-2c71-5cc4-a07b-43b3e6924efc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "1b06fac7-46cf-532f-beb1-a72504162ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8e270a1-0c6c-5922-ad57-e71feba6121f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86350/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-86350/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" "q-86350/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" "q-86350/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-86350/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-86350/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86350" :question/id #uuid "fb378625-ff34-5649-9eb8-1bcb7d6bde31" :question/math-academy-id "q-86350" :question/problem "The following table shows the velocity of a plane during a $20$-minute trip.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{minutes})$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)\\,(\\text{kilometers/minute})$ | $17$ | $25$ | $27$ | $k$ | $18$ |\n\nIf the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance traveled during this period has a value of  $450\\,\\text{km}$, what is the value of $k?$\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the velocity-time graph.*" :question/worked-solution "The area $A$ under the curve $y=v(t)$ can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{v(5)+v(10)+v(15)+v(20)}})\\cdot {{Δt}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $v(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)$ | $25$ | $27$ | $k$ | $18$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(25+27+k+18)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5(k+70) \\\\  & =5k+350\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance traveled during the $20$ minute period. Since we are given that the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance is $450\\,\\text{km},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5k+350 & =450 \\\\ 5k & =450-350 \\\\ k & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\ k & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86350/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01fe05cd-8acc-5676-9328-7a26362a77d0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "30b76ce2-9d08-5ead-8903-e2bbd5860202" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "e66f5fd5-c87c-5d87-b241-8da731327115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "f26ac8fd-24e5-5b0f-a3f2-f32c565b92d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "89b3a5a4-aa1f-5236-96ba-aa2fbd44aa86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "a753eb55-eda9-5819-8868-27e498f2f52b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b44355b5-dcdc-57e1-86c4-4af0a4f69770" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115736/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-115736/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-115736/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-115736/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-115736/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-115736/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115736" :question/id #uuid "98ae4888-9f4e-5350-a6dc-7fdb91edbc7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-115736" :question/problem "The table below gives some values of a continuous function $f(x)$ on the closed interval $[-2,4].$ The right Riemann sum approximation to the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ with $3$ equal subintervals has a value of $22.$ What must be the value of $k?$\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $k$ | $5$ | $3$ |" :question/worked-solution "The area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(0)+f(2)+f(4)}})\\cdot {{Δx}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nLet's set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $k$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(k+5+3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =(k+8)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2k+16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are given that $A$ must be $22$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2k+16 & =22 \\\\ 2k & =22-16 \\\\ k & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ k & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115736/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01fe05cd-8acc-5676-9328-7a26362a77d0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346442/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "a1e61861-8ff6-5e8d-b394-aee184004b21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346442/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "d9f77e0b-032d-577c-adde-d2eb73981d95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346442/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "85488c99-3ebe-5fd1-b862-8f9193f3487d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346442/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-346442/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-346442/field-1/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346442" :question/id #uuid "a2a1eaff-a513-598a-8f28-b6c62e22c235" :question/math-academy-id "q-346442" :question/problem "| $x$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $7$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $4$ | $2$ | $k$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above gives the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ on the closed interval $[-1,11]$ with a regular step size. If the right Riemann sum approximation to the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ with $3$ subintervals defined by the given points has a value of $96$, then what must be the value of $k?$ \n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area $A$ under the graph can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA≈(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{⏞}{f(3)+f(7)+f(11)}})\\cdot {{Δx}_{⏟}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $f(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $7$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $2$ | $k$ | $6$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈(2+k+6)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =(k+8)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4k+32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are given that $A$ must be  $96,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4k+32 & =96 \\\\ 4k & =96-32 \\\\ k & =\\frac{64}{4} \\\\ k & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346442/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01fe05cd-8acc-5676-9328-7a26362a77d0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346442"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346467/field-1/47de3feb4199e6a535715e39200236dd11c16e024516e57b517b161cf5502136" :answer/id #uuid "61aa31d3-f7d8-5311-bfa1-14c4e61efbab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26.50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346467/field-1/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "64ed92e1-33fe-57b7-82a6-303906358490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346467/field-1/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "d330d367-42c2-5cf4-bd05-dbbb64f422cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346467/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "a32a2d1d-abc7-5036-b42d-6acdab958a0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346467/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "40bcf070-